return {h=9,w=455,cr=190,hc=20,bh=70,gr="slow",eg={"water3"},st={40,40,35,50,100,70},ab={{29,0},{64,0},{44,1}},genus={en="Jellyfish Pokémon",es="Pokémon Medusa",pt="Pokémon Água-viva"},flavor={en={[1]="Drifts in shallow seas. Anglers who hook them by accident are often punished by its stinging acid.",[2]="Drifts in shallow seas. Anglers who hook them by accident are often punished by its stinging acid.",[3]="It can sometimes be found all dry and shriveled up on a beach. Toss it back into the sea to revive it.",[4]="When the tide goes out, dehydrated TENTACOOL remains can be found washed up on the shore.",[5]="It drifts aimlessly in waves. Very difficult to see in water, it may not be noticed until it stings.",[6]="As it floats along on the waves, it uses its toxic feelers to stab anything it touches.",[7]="TENTACOOL’s body is largely composed of water. If it is removed from the sea, it dries up like parchment. If this Pokémon happens to become dehydrated, put it back into the sea.",[8]="TENTACOOL absorbs sunlight and refracts it using water inside its body to convert it into beam energy. This Pokémon shoots beams from its crystal-like eyes.",[9]="Its body is almost entirely composed of water. It ensnares its foe with its two long tentacles, then stabs with the poison stingers at their tips.",[10]="Its eyes are as transparent as crystals. From them, it shoots mysterious beams of light.",[11]="Drifts in shallow seas. Anglers who hook them by accident are often punished by their stingers.",[12]="Its body is virtually composed of water. It shoots strange beams from its crystal-like eyes.",[13]="It drifts in sea currents. Countless fishermen are hurt by its poison stingers.",[14]="Because its body is almost entirely composed of water, it shrivels up if it is washed ashore.",[15]="When the tide goes out, dehydrated TENTACOOL remains can be found washed up on the shore.",[16]="It drifts aimlessly in waves. Very difficult to see in water, it may not be noticed until it stings.",[17]="Because its body is almost entirely composed of water, it shrivels up if it is washed ashore.",[18]="Because its body is almost entirely composed of water, it shrivels up if it is washed ashore.",[21]="Because its body is almost entirely composed of water, it shrivels up if it is washed ashore.",[22]="Because its body is almost entirely composed of water, it shrivels up if it is washed ashore.",[23]="Its body is virtually composed of water. It shoots strange beams from its crystal-like eyes.",[24]="Drifts in shallow seas. Anglers who hook them by accident are often punished by their stingers.",[25]="Tentacool’s body is largely composed of water. If it is removed from the sea, it dries up like parchment. If this Pokémon happens to become dehydrated, put it back into the sea.",[26]="Tentacool absorbs sunlight and refracts it using water inside its body to convert it into beam energy. This Pokémon shoots beams from the small round organ above its eyes.",[27]="They can be found lying dehydrated on beaches, but they are often still alive. When soaked in water, they will revive.",[28]="It drifts in shallow seas, such as the areas near beaches. If you get bitten or stabbed by its toxic tentacles, rush to the hospital.",[29]="It drifts through the sea searching for prey. Its poisonous tentacles break off sometimes, but after a while, they grow back.",[30]="Its body is 99% water. The remaining 1% contains the organ that makes its poison.",[31]="It can sometimes be found all dry and shriveled up on a beach. Toss it back into the sea to revive it.",[32]="It can sometimes be found all dry and shriveled up on a beach. Toss it back into the sea to revive it.",[33]="Tentacool is not a particularly strong swimmer. It drifts across the surface of shallow seas as it searches for prey.",[34]="This Pokémon is mostly made of water. A Tentacool out in the ocean is very hard to spot, because its body blends in with the sea.",[39]="They fire beams from the glassy, magenta orbs that resemble eyes atop their heads, and they drift in shallow seas. During low tide, they can sometimes be found on beaches, desiccated."},es={[23]="Su cuerpo se compone casi en exclusiva de agua. Lanza extraños rayos con sus ojos cristalinos.",[24]="Va a la deriva a poca profundidad. Si es pescado por accidente, el castigo será su punzante ácido.",[25]="Tentacool está compuesto en su mayor parte por agua. Si se le saca del mar, se secará y se quedará acartonado. Si este Pokémon se deshidrata, hay que echarlo inmediatamente de vuelta al mar.",[26]="Tentacool absorbe luz solar, la refracta a través del agua que tiene en su interior y la convierte en un rayo de energía. Este Pokémon tiene un órgano que parece de cristal sobre los ojos por el cual dispara los rayos.",[27]="A veces es posible encontrarlos deshidratados en la playa, pero, si se los pone en remojo, volverán a henchirse de vida.",[28]="Suele rondar las aguas poco profundas de la orilla. Sus tentáculos son muy venenosos y, en caso de picadura, hay que correr al hospital.",[29]="Ronda las costas en busca de presas. Si pierde alguno de sus tentáculos venenosos, le volverá a crecer al cabo del tiempo.",[30]="Su cuerpo está compuesto de agua en un 99%. El 1% restante es el órgano que segrega sus toxinas.",[31]="A veces pueden encontrarse deshidratados en las playas, pero reviven al sumergirlos de nuevo en el agua.",[32]="A veces pueden encontrarse deshidratados en las playas, pero reviven al sumergirlos de nuevo en el agua.",[33]="Sus facultades natatorias son más bien escasas, por lo que se limita a flotar a la deriva en aguas poco profundas en busca de alimento.",[34]="Su cuerpo está compuesto casi por completo de agua, por lo que resulta muy difícil distinguirlo cuando está sumergido en el mar."},pt="Disparam raios das esferas magenta e vítreas, parecidas com olhos, no topo da cabeça, e flutuam em mares rasos. Na maré baixa, às vezes são encontrados ressecados nas praias."},evo={{s=72},{s=73,from=72,c={{t="l